Global Supply Solutions is actively exploring the integration of autonomous delivery vehicles (ADVs) into its last-mile delivery strategy. These self-driving vehicles can optimize delivery routes, reduce labor costs, and enhance safety. For instance, trials with autonomous vans have shown a reduction in delivery times by up to 20%, demonstrating the potential for significant efficiency gains. Additionally, partnerships with technology firms specializing in autonomous vehicle development are underway to ensure successful implementation.

#### 17.2 Drones for Delivery

The use of drones for last-mile deliveries is gaining traction in urban environments where traffic congestion can hinder traditional delivery methods. Global Supply Solutions is piloting drone delivery services in select metropolitan areas, targeting smaller packages and urgent deliveries. Initial tests have shown that drones can complete deliveries within a 5-mile radius in under 30 minutes, significantly improving customer satisfaction and operational efficiency.

#### 17.3 Smart Lockers and Pickup Points

To enhance customer convenience and reduce delivery costs, the company is implementing a network of smart lockers and pickup points throughout urban areas. Customers can choose to have their packages delivered to these secure locations, allowing for flexible pickup times. This innovation not only reduces the number of failed delivery attempts but also decreases the overall carbon footprint associated with multiple delivery trips.

